// ─────────────────────── PRACTICE TEST 7 · R&W M1 (27) ───────────────────────
const T7_RW_M1: SatQuestion[] = [
  { id: "t7rw1-1", section: "rw", domain: "Craft and Structure", difficulty: "med", passage: "The chef's signature sauce was praised for its ______ flavor, balancing sweet, sour, and savory notes in a single spoonful.", prompt: "Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word?", type: "mcq", choices: ["complex", "bland", "sour", "watery"], correct: 0, explanation: "Balancing several notes at once describes a \"complex\" flavor." },
  { id: "t7rw1-2", section: "rw", domain: "Standard English Conventions", difficulty: "med", passage: "The flock of geese ______ migrating south earlier than usual this autumn.", prompt: "Which choice conforms to the conventions of Standard English?", type: "mcq", choices: ["is", "are", "have been", "were"], correct: 0, explanation: "The subject is the singular collective noun \"flock,\" so \"is.\"" },
  { id: "t7rw1-3", section: "rw", domain: "Information and Ideas", difficulty: "hard", passage: "Mycorrhizal fungi link the roots of neighboring trees underground, ferrying water and nutrients between them in exchange for sugars the trees produce.", prompt: "Which choice best states the main idea of the text?", type: "mcq", choices: ["Fungi and trees trade resources through an underground network.", "Trees grow best when isolated from fungi.", "Fungi take nutrients from trees without giving anything back.", "Trees produce no sugars of their own."], correct: 0, explanation: "The fungi move water and nutrients in exchange for sugars — a mutual trade (choice A)." },
  { id: "t7rw1-4", section: "rw", domain: "Expression of Ideas", difficulty: "med", passage: "The bridge was nearing the end of its safe lifespan. ______, engineers recommended replacing it within the decade.", prompt: "Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?", type: "mcq", choices: ["Nevertheless", "Consequently", "However", "In contrast"], correct: 1, explanation: "The recommendation follows from the aging bridge — \"Consequently.\"" },
  { id: "t7rw1-5", section: "rw", domain: "Standard English Conventions", difficulty: "med", passage: "The recipe calls for three spices ______ cumin, coriander, and turmeric.", prompt: "Which choice conforms to the conventions of Standard English?", type: "mcq", choices: ["spices, ", "spices: ", "spices; ", "spices "], correct: 1, explanation: "A colon introduces the list that explains \"three spices.\"" },
  { id: "t7rw1-6", section: "rw", domain: "Craft and Structure", difficulty: "med", passage: "Her travel journal was unusually ______, recording even the color of each train ticket she collected.", prompt: "Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word?", type: "mcq", choices: ["thorough", "careless", "brief", "vague"], correct: 0, explanation: "Recording tiny details shows the journal was \"thorough.\"" },
  { id: "t7rw1-7", section: "rw", domain: "Information and Ideas", difficulty: "med", passage: "The grant funds research projects led only by scientists who have held a doctorate for at least five years; newer doctorate-holders are ineligible.", prompt: "Which statement is best supported by the text?", type: "mcq", choices: ["A scientist who earned a doctorate two years ago cannot lead a funded project.", "Every scientist qualifies for the grant.", "The grant funds projects led by students.", "Scientists with no doctorate are eligible."], correct: 0, explanation: "Fewer than five years since the doctorate means ineligibility (choice A)." },
  { id: "t7rw1-8", section: "rw", domain: "Expression of Ideas", difficulty: "med", passage: "The orchestra rehearsed for months. ______, it added a guest soloist for the final concert.", prompt: "Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?", type: "mcq", choices: ["However", "In addition", "Otherwise", "Instead"], correct: 1, explanation: "A further preparation is added — \"In addition.\"" },
  { id: "t7rw1-9", section: "rw", domain: "Craft and Structure", difficulty: "med", passage: "Critics called the documentary ______, noting that it raised pointed questions without ever pretending to answer them.", prompt: "Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word?", type: "mcq", choices: ["provocative", "tedious", "conclusive", "soothing"], correct: 0, explanation: "Raising pointed questions makes a film \"provocative.\"" },
  { id: "t7rw1-10", section: "rw", domain: "Information and Ideas", difficulty: "med", passage: "Octopuses can change both the color and the texture of their skin in under a second, blending almost perfectly with coral, sand, or rock.", prompt: "Which choice best states the main idea of the text?", type: "mcq", choices: ["Octopuses camouflage by rapidly altering their skin's color and texture.", "Octopuses cannot change their appearance.", "Octopuses are visible to all predators.", "Octopuses live only on sand."], correct: 0, explanation: "Rapidly changing color and texture to blend in is camouflage (choice A)." },
  { id: "t7rw1-11", section: "rw", domain: "Standard English Conventions", difficulty: "med", passage: "Each of the runners ______ expected to finish the marathon within four hours.", prompt: "Which choice conforms to the conventions of Standard English?", type: "mcq", choices: ["is", "are", "were", "have been"], correct: 0, explanation: "\"Each\" is singular, so the verb is \"is.\"" },
  { id: "t7rw1-12", section: "rw", domain: "Expression of Ideas", difficulty: "med", passage: "The startup's first app failed to attract users. ______, its founders learned lessons that shaped a far more successful second product.", prompt: "Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?", type: "mcq", choices: ["Still", "For instance", "Therefore", "In short"], correct: 0, explanation: "A failure that nonetheless taught useful lessons is a contrast — \"Still.\"" },
  { id: "t7rw1-13", section: "rw", domain: "Information and Ideas", difficulty: "hard", passage: "Survey results showed satisfaction at 62% in the city center, 78% in the suburbs, and 81% in rural areas of the county.", prompt: "Which statement is best supported by the data?", type: "mcq", choices: ["Satisfaction was lowest in the city center.", "Satisfaction was highest in the city center.", "Suburban satisfaction exceeded rural satisfaction.", "All three areas reported identical satisfaction."], correct: 0, explanation: "62% (city center) is the smallest of the three figures (choice A)." },
  { id: "t7rw1-14", section: "rw", domain: "Standard English Conventions", difficulty: "med", passage: "The museum acquired a painting ______ had been hidden in a private collection for a century.", prompt: "Which choice conforms to the conventions of Standard English?", type: "mcq", choices: ["that", "what", "where", "and it"], correct: 0, explanation: "The relative pronoun \"that\" introduces the clause modifying \"painting.\"" },
  { id: "t7rw1-15", section: "rw", domain: "Craft and Structure", difficulty: "med", passage: "Walking onto the stage, ______ the bright lights made the singer pause for a moment.", prompt: "Which choice avoids a dangling modifier and conforms to Standard English?", type: "mcq", choices: ["walking onto the stage, the bright lights made the singer pause", "the singer paused as she walked onto the stage, blinded by the bright lights", "the bright lights, walking onto the stage, made her pause", "pausing, the bright lights blinded the singer onto the stage"], correct: 1, explanation: "Only choice B places the person doing the walking (the singer) right after the modifier." },
  { id: "t7rw1-16", section: "rw", domain: "Information and Ideas", difficulty: "med", passage: "Researchers argue that frequent note-taking by hand, though slower than typing, leads to deeper understanding because writers must summarize rather than transcribe.", prompt: "Which finding, if true, would most strengthen the researchers' claim?", type: "mcq", choices: ["Students who handwrote notes scored higher on conceptual questions than those who typed.", "Typing notes is faster than writing them by hand.", "Most students prefer typing to handwriting.", "Handwriting and typing produce the same word count."], correct: 0, explanation: "Higher conceptual scores for handwriters directly support the deeper-understanding claim (choice A)." },
  { id: "t7rw1-17", section: "rw", domain: "Standard English Conventions", difficulty: "med", passage: "The architect, along with her two assistants, ______ presenting the final plans tomorrow.", prompt: "Which choice conforms to the conventions of Standard English?", type: "mcq", choices: ["is", "are", "were", "have been"], correct: 0, explanation: "The subject is the singular \"architect\"; \"along with\" phrases do not change the number, so \"is.\"" },
  { id: "t7rw1-18", section: "rw", domain: "Expression of Ideas", difficulty: "med", passage: "A scientist wants to emphasize that two unrelated experiments reached the same conclusion. ______, both teams found that the enzyme degraded above 40°C.", prompt: "Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?", type: "mcq", choices: ["By contrast", "Notably", "However", "Otherwise"], correct: 1, explanation: "\"Notably\" highlights the striking agreement between the two experiments." },
  { id: "t7rw1-19", section: "rw", domain: "Craft and Structure", difficulty: "hard", passage: "The poem's final stanza is deliberately ______: each reader leaves with a different sense of whether the speaker has found peace.", prompt: "Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word?", type: "mcq", choices: ["open-ended", "literal", "repetitive", "cheerful"], correct: 0, explanation: "Allowing different interpretations makes the stanza \"open-ended.\"" },
  { id: "t7rw1-20", section: "rw", domain: "Information and Ideas", difficulty: "med", passage: "The new tax credit is available only to households that installed solar panels after 2023 and that earn below the county median income.", prompt: "Which household clearly qualifies for the credit?", type: "mcq", choices: ["A below-median-income household that installed panels in 2024.", "A high-income household that installed panels in 2024.", "A below-median-income household that installed panels in 2019.", "A household that has never installed panels."], correct: 0, explanation: "Both conditions — post-2023 install and below-median income — are met only in choice A." },
  { id: "t7rw1-21", section: "rw", domain: "Standard English Conventions", difficulty: "med", passage: "The volunteers cleaned the riverbank ______ they planted native grasses along the slope.", prompt: "Which choice conforms to the conventions of Standard English?", type: "mcq", choices: ["riverbank, and then", "riverbank and, then", "riverbank then", "riverbank, then"], correct: 0, explanation: "A comma plus the coordinating conjunction \"and\" correctly joins the two independent clauses." },
  { id: "t7rw1-22", section: "rw", domain: "Craft and Structure", difficulty: "med", passage: "Although she was known for her ______ remarks, the columnist could be surprisingly gentle when reviewing first novels.", prompt: "Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word?", type: "mcq", choices: ["caustic", "tender", "hesitant", "muted"], correct: 0, explanation: "The contrast with \"gentle\" implies her usual remarks were \"caustic\" (biting)." },
  { id: "t7rw1-23", section: "rw", domain: "Information and Ideas", difficulty: "med", passage: "A historian notes that medieval towns built near rivers grew faster than inland towns, attributing the gap to easier trade and transport.", prompt: "Which choice best describes the historian's explanation?", type: "mcq", choices: ["River access aided trade and transport, fueling faster growth.", "Inland towns had better trade routes.", "Rivers slowed the growth of nearby towns.", "Town location had no effect on growth."], correct: 0, explanation: "The historian attributes faster growth to river-enabled trade and transport (choice A)." },
  { id: "t7rw1-24", section: "rw", domain: "Standard English Conventions", difficulty: "med", passage: "The committee postponed its decision ______ it lacked the data needed to choose between the two sites.", prompt: "Which choice conforms to the conventions of Standard English?", type: "mcq", choices: ["decision because", "decision, because", "decision; because", "decision: because"], correct: 0, explanation: "No comma is needed before \"because\" when the dependent clause follows the main clause." },
  { id: "t7rw1-25", section: "rw", domain: "Expression of Ideas", difficulty: "med", passage: "The factory cut its energy use by half. ______, it reduced its annual operating costs by nearly a million dollars.", prompt: "Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?", type: "mcq", choices: ["As a result", "Nevertheless", "For example", "On the other hand"], correct: 0, explanation: "Lower costs follow from cutting energy use — cause and effect, \"As a result.\"" },
  { id: "t7rw1-26", section: "rw", domain: "Craft and Structure", difficulty: "med", passage: "The mentor offered ______ advice, the kind a student could actually apply the very next morning.", prompt: "Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word?", type: "mcq", choices: ["practical", "abstract", "confusing", "irrelevant"], correct: 0, explanation: "Advice that can be applied immediately is \"practical.\"" },
  { id: "t7rw1-27", section: "rw", domain: "Information and Ideas", difficulty: "hard", passage: "A field study found that wolves' return to a valley reduced the elk population, which in turn allowed young willow trees — once overgrazed — to recover along the streams.", prompt: "Which choice best states the main idea of the text?", type: "mcq", choices: ["Restoring wolves triggered a chain of effects that helped willows recover.", "Wolves directly planted the willow trees.", "Elk populations grew after the wolves returned.", "Willows declined once the wolves arrived."], correct: 0, explanation: "Wolves reduced elk, which let overgrazed willows recover — a chain effect (choice A)." },
];

// ─────────────────────── PRACTICE TEST 7 · R&W M2 easy (27) ──────────────────
const T7_RW_M2E: SatQuestion[] = [
  { id: "t7rw2e-1", section: "rw", domain: "Craft and Structure", difficulty: "easy", passage: "The soup was too ______, so I added some cold water to cool it down.", prompt: "Which choice completes the text with the most logical word?", type: "mcq", choices: ["hot", "sweet", "blue", "loud"], correct: 0, explanation: "Cooling it with cold water means the soup was \"hot.\"" },
  { id: "t7rw2e-2", section: "rw", domain: "Standard English Conventions", difficulty: "easy", passage: "The two cats ______ sleeping on the warm windowsill.", prompt: "Which choice conforms to the conventions of Standard English?", type: "mcq", choices: ["is", "are", "was", "am"], correct: 1, explanation: "\"Two cats\" is plural, so \"are.\"" },
  { id: "t7rw2e-3", section: "rw", domain: "Information and Ideas", difficulty: "easy", passage: "Penguins cannot fly, but their wings act like flippers that help them swim quickly through the water.", prompt: "Which choice best states the main idea of the text?", type: "mcq", choices: ["Penguins use their wings to swim rather than to fly.", "Penguins fly long distances every year.", "Penguins cannot move in water.", "Penguins have no wings at all."], correct: 0, explanation: "Their wings act as flippers for swimming (choice A)." },
  { id: "t7rw2e-4", section: "rw", domain: "Expression of Ideas", difficulty: "easy", passage: "The library was closing in ten minutes. ______, I quickly checked out my book.", prompt: "Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?", type: "mcq", choices: ["For example", "So", "However", "Meanwhile"], correct: 1, explanation: "The closing time is the reason I hurried — \"So.\"" },
  { id: "t7rw2e-5", section: "rw", domain: "Standard English Conventions", difficulty: "easy", passage: "Last week we ______ a movie at the new theater downtown.", prompt: "Which choice conforms to the conventions of Standard English?", type: "mcq", choices: ["watch", "watches", "watched", "watching"], correct: 2, explanation: "\"Last week\" requires the past tense \"watched.\"" },
  { id: "t7rw2e-6", section: "rw", domain: "Craft and Structure", difficulty: "easy", passage: "The garden was full of ______ flowers in red, yellow, and purple.", prompt: "Which choice completes the text with the most logical word?", type: "mcq", choices: ["colorful", "dull", "broken", "empty"], correct: 0, explanation: "Many bright colors make the flowers \"colorful.\"" },
  { id: "t7rw2e-7", section: "rw", domain: "Information and Ideas", difficulty: "easy", passage: "Recycling paper saves trees, reduces waste in landfills, and uses less energy than making new paper.", prompt: "Which choice best states the main idea of the text?", type: "mcq", choices: ["Recycling paper offers several environmental benefits.", "Recycling paper harms the environment.", "Recycling paper only saves trees.", "Making new paper is always better."], correct: 0, explanation: "Three benefits are listed — choice A." },
  { id: "t7rw2e-8", section: "rw", domain: "Standard English Conventions", difficulty: "easy", passage: "She waited for ______ hour before the bus finally arrived.", prompt: "Which choice conforms to the conventions of Standard English?", type: "mcq", choices: ["a", "an", "the only", "some"], correct: 1, explanation: "\"Hour\" begins with a silent h (a vowel sound), so \"an.\"" },
  { id: "t7rw2e-9", section: "rw", domain: "Craft and Structure", difficulty: "easy", passage: "The test was ______, so most students finished early and felt confident.", prompt: "Which choice completes the text with the most logical word?", type: "mcq", choices: ["easy", "impossible", "endless", "frightening"], correct: 0, explanation: "Finishing early and feeling confident means the test was \"easy.\"" },
  { id: "t7rw2e-10", section: "rw", domain: "Standard English Conventions", difficulty: "easy", passage: "My brother and I ______ going to the beach this weekend.", prompt: "Which choice conforms to the conventions of Standard English?", type: "mcq", choices: ["is", "are", "was", "am"], correct: 1, explanation: "The compound subject \"my brother and I\" is plural, so \"are.\"" },
  { id: "t7rw2e-11", section: "rw", domain: "Information and Ideas", difficulty: "easy", passage: "Camels store fat in their humps, which their bodies can use for energy when food and water are scarce.", prompt: "Which choice best states the main idea of the text?", type: "mcq", choices: ["A camel's hump stores fat the camel can use when resources are scarce.", "A camel's hump stores water only.", "Camels never need food.", "Camels cannot survive in deserts."], correct: 0, explanation: "The hump stores fat used for energy when food and water are scarce (choice A)." },
  { id: "t7rw2e-12", section: "rw", domain: "Expression of Ideas", difficulty: "easy", passage: "It started to snow heavily. ______, the school announced an early dismissal.", prompt: "Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?", type: "mcq", choices: ["However", "As a result", "For example", "Instead"], correct: 1, explanation: "The early dismissal follows from the snow — \"As a result.\"" },
  { id: "t7rw2e-13", section: "rw", domain: "Standard English Conventions", difficulty: "easy", passage: "Yesterday the team ______ its first game of the season.", prompt: "Which choice conforms to the conventions of Standard English?", type: "mcq", choices: ["win", "wins", "won", "winning"], correct: 2, explanation: "\"Yesterday\" requires the past tense \"won.\"" },
  { id: "t7rw2e-14", section: "rw", domain: "Craft and Structure", difficulty: "easy", passage: "After running the race, the athlete felt ______ and sat down to rest.", prompt: "Which choice completes the text with the most logical word?", type: "mcq", choices: ["exhausted", "energetic", "bored", "amused"], correct: 0, explanation: "Needing to rest after a race means the athlete was \"exhausted.\"" },
  { id: "t7rw2e-15", section: "rw", domain: "Information and Ideas", difficulty: "easy", passage: "The store is open from 9 a.m. to 6 p.m. on weekdays but stays closed on Sundays.", prompt: "Which statement is best supported by the text?", type: "mcq", choices: ["You cannot shop at the store on Sunday.", "The store opens at midnight.", "The store is open every day.", "The store closes at 9 a.m."], correct: 0, explanation: "The store is closed on Sundays (choice A)." },
  { id: "t7rw2e-16", section: "rw", domain: "Standard English Conventions", difficulty: "easy", passage: "The dog wagged ______ tail when its owner came home.", prompt: "Which choice conforms to the conventions of Standard English?", type: "mcq", choices: ["its", "it's", "their", "they're"], correct: 0, explanation: "The singular possessive \"its\" matches the singular \"dog.\"" },
  { id: "t7rw2e-17", section: "rw", domain: "Expression of Ideas", difficulty: "easy", passage: "Many plants need sunlight to grow. ______, sunflowers turn to face the sun throughout the day.", prompt: "Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?", type: "mcq", choices: ["For example", "However", "Instead", "Otherwise"], correct: 0, explanation: "Sunflowers are an example of a plant that follows the sun — \"For example.\"" },
  { id: "t7rw2e-18", section: "rw", domain: "Craft and Structure", difficulty: "easy", passage: "The room was very ______, so we turned on every lamp we could find.", prompt: "Which choice completes the text with the most logical word?", type: "mcq", choices: ["dark", "bright", "warm", "loud"], correct: 0, explanation: "Turning on lamps means the room was \"dark.\"" },
  { id: "t7rw2e-19", section: "rw", domain: "Standard English Conventions", difficulty: "easy", passage: "The boxes ______ stacked neatly against the back wall.", prompt: "Which choice conforms to the conventions of Standard English?", type: "mcq", choices: ["is", "are", "was", "am"], correct: 1, explanation: "\"Boxes\" is plural, so \"are.\"" },
  { id: "t7rw2e-20", section: "rw", domain: "Information and Ideas", difficulty: "easy", passage: "Honey never spoils; jars of it thousands of years old have been found still safe to eat.", prompt: "Which choice best states the main idea of the text?", type: "mcq", choices: ["Honey can remain edible for a very long time.", "Honey spoils within days.", "Honey is unsafe to eat.", "Honey cannot be stored in jars."], correct: 0, explanation: "Ancient honey is still edible — honey lasts a very long time (choice A)." },
  { id: "t7rw2e-21", section: "rw", domain: "Expression of Ideas", difficulty: "easy", passage: "We wanted to leave early. ______, traffic delayed us by an hour.", prompt: "Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?", type: "mcq", choices: ["However", "Therefore", "For example", "Similarly"], correct: 0, explanation: "Wanting to leave early but being delayed is a contrast — \"However.\"" },
  { id: "t7rw2e-22", section: "rw", domain: "Standard English Conventions", difficulty: "easy", passage: "Next summer my family ______ to visit the national park.", prompt: "Which choice conforms to the conventions of Standard English?", type: "mcq", choices: ["plan", "plans", "planned", "planning"], correct: 1, explanation: "The singular \"family\" takes \"plans,\" and \"next summer\" fits the present-as-future use." },
  { id: "t7rw2e-23", section: "rw", domain: "Craft and Structure", difficulty: "easy", passage: "The new phone is very ______; it weighs less than a deck of cards.", prompt: "Which choice completes the text with the most logical word?", type: "mcq", choices: ["light", "heavy", "loud", "wide"], correct: 0, explanation: "Weighing very little means the phone is \"light.\"" },
  { id: "t7rw2e-24", section: "rw", domain: "Information and Ideas", difficulty: "easy", passage: "Reading aloud to young children helps them learn new words, recognize letters, and enjoy stories.", prompt: "Which choice best states the main idea of the text?", type: "mcq", choices: ["Reading aloud to children supports their learning in several ways.", "Reading aloud confuses children.", "Children should never be read to.", "Reading aloud only teaches letters."], correct: 0, explanation: "Three benefits are listed — choice A." },
  { id: "t7rw2e-25", section: "rw", domain: "Standard English Conventions", difficulty: "easy", passage: "She bought ______ umbrella before the storm arrived.", prompt: "Which choice conforms to the conventions of Standard English?", type: "mcq", choices: ["a", "an", "the only", "some"], correct: 1, explanation: "\"Umbrella\" begins with a vowel sound, so \"an.\"" },
  { id: "t7rw2e-26", section: "rw", domain: "Expression of Ideas", difficulty: "easy", passage: "The recipe was simple to follow. ______, it took only twenty minutes to make.", prompt: "Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?", type: "mcq", choices: ["In addition", "However", "Instead", "Otherwise"], correct: 0, explanation: "A second good point is added — \"In addition.\"" },
  { id: "t7rw2e-27", section: "rw", domain: "Craft and Structure", difficulty: "easy", passage: "The crowd was ______ when the home team scored the winning goal.", prompt: "Which choice completes the text with the most logical word?", type: "mcq", choices: ["thrilled", "silent", "bored", "tired"], correct: 0, explanation: "A winning goal makes the home crowd \"thrilled.\"" },
];

// ─────────────────────── PRACTICE TEST 7 · R&W M2 hard (27) ──────────────────
const T7_RW_M2H: SatQuestion[] = [
  { id: "t7rw2h-1", section: "rw", domain: "Craft and Structure", difficulty: "hard", passage: "The senator's apology was so ______ that it managed to acknowledge the harm while quietly denying any personal fault.", prompt: "Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word?", type: "mcq", choices: ["equivocal", "sincere", "blunt", "wholehearted"], correct: 0, explanation: "Acknowledging harm while denying fault is \"equivocal\" (ambiguous, hedging)." },
  { id: "t7rw2h-2", section: "rw", domain: "Information and Ideas", difficulty: "hard", passage: "The essay devotes its first half to vivid anecdotes before stepping back, in the second half, to draw a single general principle from them.", prompt: "Which choice best describes the structure of the text?", type: "mcq", choices: ["It moves from specific examples to a broader generalization.", "It begins with a thesis and never supports it.", "It lists definitions without examples.", "It repeats one anecdote throughout."], correct: 0, explanation: "Anecdotes first, then a general principle — specific to general (choice A)." },
  { id: "t7rw2h-3", section: "rw", domain: "Information and Ideas", difficulty: "hard", passage: "A battery held 92% capacity after 100 charge cycles, 90% after 200 cycles, and 75% after 500 cycles.", prompt: "Which statement is best supported by the data?", type: "mcq", choices: ["Capacity fell more steeply between 200 and 500 cycles than before.", "Capacity rose as cycles increased.", "Capacity stayed exactly constant.", "The battery was dead by 200 cycles."], correct: 0, explanation: "92 to 90 over 100 cycles is gentle; 90 to 75 over 300 cycles is much steeper per cycle (choice A)." },
  { id: "t7rw2h-4", section: "rw", domain: "Expression of Ideas", difficulty: "hard", passage: "The proposal would cut commute times dramatically. ______, it would route the new highway through a protected wetland.", prompt: "Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?", type: "mcq", choices: ["Therefore", "However", "Likewise", "Accordingly"], correct: 1, explanation: "A benefit followed by a serious drawback is a contrast — \"However.\"" },
  { id: "t7rw2h-5", section: "rw", domain: "Standard English Conventions", difficulty: "hard", passage: "The workshop trains volunteers to plan events, to manage budgets, and ______ donors effectively.", prompt: "Which choice conforms to the conventions of Standard English?", type: "mcq", choices: ["to recruit", "recruiting", "recruit", "recruited"], correct: 0, explanation: "Parallel with \"to plan\" and \"to manage\" requires \"to recruit.\"" },
  { id: "t7rw2h-6", section: "rw", domain: "Craft and Structure", difficulty: "hard", passage: "The biography refuses to ______ its subject, presenting his failures as candidly as his triumphs.", prompt: "Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word?", type: "mcq", choices: ["idealize", "criticize", "describe", "remember"], correct: 0, explanation: "Showing failures candidly means it refuses to \"idealize\" him." },
  { id: "t7rw2h-7", section: "rw", domain: "Information and Ideas", difficulty: "hard", passage: "Where the older theory treated memory as a faithful recording, the newer model casts it as an act of reconstruction shaped by present beliefs.", prompt: "Which choice best describes the main purpose of the text?", type: "mcq", choices: ["To contrast an older view of memory with a newer, reconstructive one.", "To prove memory is a perfect recording.", "To summarize only the older theory.", "To argue memory does not exist."], correct: 0, explanation: "\"Where the older … the newer …\" contrasts two models of memory (choice A)." },
  { id: "t7rw2h-8", section: "rw", domain: "Standard English Conventions", difficulty: "hard", passage: "The morning shift handled the surge of orders smoothly ______ the evening shift struggled with the very same volume.", prompt: "Which choice conforms to the conventions of Standard English?", type: "mcq", choices: ["smoothly, the", "smoothly; the", "smoothly the", "smoothly: the"], correct: 1, explanation: "Two independent clauses are joined by a semicolon." },
  { id: "t7rw2h-9", section: "rw", domain: "Craft and Structure", difficulty: "hard", passage: "Far from being ______, the author's prose is dense with allusions that reward, and sometimes demand, a second reading.", prompt: "Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word?", type: "mcq", choices: ["transparent", "intricate", "layered", "demanding"], correct: 0, explanation: "\"Far from\" signals an opposite: prose demanding rereading is the opposite of \"transparent.\"" },
  { id: "t7rw2h-10", section: "rw", domain: "Information and Ideas", difficulty: "hard", passage: "Critics claim the policy raised wages without reducing employment. Yet in the year it took effect, hiring at affected firms fell by 4%.", prompt: "Which choice best describes the function of the second sentence?", type: "mcq", choices: ["It offers evidence that complicates the critics' claim.", "It restates the critics' claim word for word.", "It confirms that employment was unaffected.", "It proposes a new policy."], correct: 0, explanation: "A drop in hiring complicates the claim that employment did not fall (choice A)." },
  { id: "t7rw2h-11", section: "rw", domain: "Standard English Conventions", difficulty: "hard", passage: "The expedition's success depended on three things ______ favorable weather, ample supplies, and an experienced guide.", prompt: "Which choice conforms to the conventions of Standard English?", type: "mcq", choices: ["things,", "things:", "things;", "things"], correct: 1, explanation: "A colon introduces the list that specifies the \"three things.\"" },
  { id: "t7rw2h-12", section: "rw", domain: "Expression of Ideas", difficulty: "hard", passage: "The model predicted the storm's path with impressive accuracy. ______, it failed to anticipate the storm's rapid intensification.", prompt: "Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?", type: "mcq", choices: ["Indeed", "Nonetheless", "Therefore", "Likewise"], correct: 1, explanation: "A success followed by a notable failure is a concession — \"Nonetheless.\"" },
  { id: "t7rw2h-13", section: "rw", domain: "Information and Ideas", difficulty: "hard", passage: "In a trial, plants given the new fertilizer grew 30% taller than untreated plants, but they also produced 20% fewer flowers.", prompt: "Which statement is best supported by the data?", type: "mcq", choices: ["The fertilizer increased height but reduced flowering.", "The fertilizer increased both height and flowering.", "The fertilizer had no measurable effect.", "Untreated plants grew taller than treated ones."], correct: 0, explanation: "Treated plants were taller (+30%) but flowered less (−20%) (choice A)." },
  { id: "t7rw2h-14", section: "rw", domain: "Standard English Conventions", difficulty: "hard", passage: "The painting that hangs above the fireplace ______ to the artist's earliest period, long before her famous murals.", prompt: "Which choice conforms to the conventions of Standard English?", type: "mcq", choices: ["belong", "belongs", "belonging", "to belong"], correct: 1, explanation: "The singular subject \"painting\" (not the plural \"murals\") takes the singular verb \"belongs.\"" },
  { id: "t7rw2h-15", section: "rw", domain: "Craft and Structure", difficulty: "hard", passage: "The diplomat's reputation for ______ — for saying precisely what was needed and not a word more — made her a sought-after negotiator.", prompt: "Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word?", type: "mcq", choices: ["concision", "verbosity", "indecision", "flattery"], correct: 0, explanation: "Saying exactly what is needed and no more is \"concision.\"" },
  { id: "t7rw2h-16", section: "rw", domain: "Information and Ideas", difficulty: "hard", passage: "The author opens by granting that early computers were enormous and unreliable, then argues that these very limitations spurred the innovations that made them small and dependable.", prompt: "Which choice best describes the text's reasoning?", type: "mcq", choices: ["It turns an apparent weakness into the source of later strengths.", "It denies that early computers had any flaws.", "It claims computers never improved.", "It lists computer prices over time."], correct: 0, explanation: "The limitations are recast as the spur for improvements (choice A)." },
  { id: "t7rw2h-17", section: "rw", domain: "Standard English Conventions", difficulty: "hard", passage: "Having trained for years on quiet mountain trails ______ the marathon's crowded city streets felt overwhelming.", prompt: "Which choice avoids a dangling modifier and conforms to Standard English?", type: "mcq", choices: ["the marathon's crowded city streets felt overwhelming", "the runner found the marathon's crowded city streets overwhelming", "overwhelming were the marathon's crowded streets", "it was overwhelming, the crowded streets"], correct: 1, explanation: "Only choice B supplies the person who did the training — \"the runner\" — after the modifier." },
  { id: "t7rw2h-18", section: "rw", domain: "Expression of Ideas", difficulty: "hard", passage: "The drug shrank tumors in the laboratory dish. ______, results in living animals were far more modest, and human trials have not yet begun.", prompt: "Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?", type: "mcq", choices: ["Consequently", "In living organisms, however", "For this reason", "Similarly"], correct: 1, explanation: "The contrast between dish results and animal results is best signaled by \"In living organisms, however.\"" },
  { id: "t7rw2h-19", section: "rw", domain: "Craft and Structure", difficulty: "hard", passage: "The critic praised the album's ______ qualities, noting how a single melodic phrase resurfaces, transformed, in nearly every track.", prompt: "Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word?", type: "mcq", choices: ["unifying", "discordant", "random", "monotonous"], correct: 0, explanation: "A phrase recurring across tracks gives the album \"unifying\" qualities." },
  { id: "t7rw2h-20", section: "rw", domain: "Information and Ideas", difficulty: "hard", passage: "Across four cities, libraries that extended their evening hours saw checkouts rise by an average of 18%, while those that kept the same hours saw no change.", prompt: "Which claim is best supported by the data?", type: "mcq", choices: ["Extending evening hours was associated with higher checkouts.", "Shorter hours raised checkouts.", "Library hours had no relationship to checkouts.", "All libraries kept the same hours."], correct: 0, explanation: "Libraries that extended hours saw an 18% rise; others saw none (choice A)." },
  { id: "t7rw2h-21", section: "rw", domain: "Standard English Conventions", difficulty: "hard", passage: "The novelist's early stories — sharp, spare, and quietly funny ______ already showed the voice that her later work would refine.", prompt: "Which choice conforms to the conventions of Standard English?", type: "mcq", choices: ["stories —", "stories,", "stories", "stories;"], correct: 0, explanation: "A pair of dashes sets off the interrupting description; the second dash closes it." },
  { id: "t7rw2h-22", section: "rw", domain: "Craft and Structure", difficulty: "hard", passage: "The committee dismissed the warning as ______, only to watch the predicted shortage materialize within months.", prompt: "Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word?", type: "mcq", choices: ["alarmist", "prescient", "accurate", "urgent"], correct: 0, explanation: "Dismissing a warning that then comes true means they wrongly judged it \"alarmist.\"" },
  { id: "t7rw2h-23", section: "rw", domain: "Information and Ideas", difficulty: "hard", passage: "One scholar argues the city declined because of trade disruption; another insists the cause was a series of droughts. A third proposes that the two causes reinforced each other.", prompt: "Which choice best describes the third scholar's position?", type: "mcq", choices: ["The two proposed causes worked together to produce the decline.", "Neither trade nor drought played any role.", "Only trade disruption mattered.", "The city never actually declined."], correct: 0, explanation: "The third scholar says the causes \"reinforced each other\" (choice A)." },
  { id: "t7rw2h-24", section: "rw", domain: "Standard English Conventions", difficulty: "hard", passage: "The engineers redesigned the valve ______ the original had failed under high pressure during testing.", prompt: "Which choice conforms to the conventions of Standard English?", type: "mcq", choices: ["valve, the", "valve; the", "valve the", "valve: the"], correct: 1, explanation: "Two independent clauses are correctly joined by a semicolon." },
  { id: "t7rw2h-25", section: "rw", domain: "Expression of Ideas", difficulty: "hard", passage: "The author wants to stress that the reform's benefits were unevenly shared. ______, wealthy districts gained new schools while poorer ones saw little change.", prompt: "Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?", type: "mcq", choices: ["Specifically", "In contrast", "Nevertheless", "Otherwise"], correct: 0, explanation: "The second sentence gives a specific illustration of uneven benefits — \"Specifically.\"" },
  { id: "t7rw2h-26", section: "rw", domain: "Craft and Structure", difficulty: "hard", passage: "Rather than offering a tidy resolution, the playwright leaves the central conflict ______, trusting the audience to weigh the competing claims.", prompt: "Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word?", type: "mcq", choices: ["unresolved", "settled", "trivial", "decided"], correct: 0, explanation: "Declining a tidy resolution leaves the conflict \"unresolved.\"" },
  { id: "t7rw2h-27", section: "rw", domain: "Information and Ideas", difficulty: "hard", passage: "The researcher concedes that her sample was small, but she argues that the effect she found was so large and consistent that it merits a larger follow-up study.", prompt: "Which choice best describes the researcher's reasoning?", type: "mcq", choices: ["She acknowledges a limitation while defending the result's importance.", "She claims her study is flawless.", "She abandons her finding entirely.", "She argues no further study is needed."], correct: 0, explanation: "She admits the small sample yet defends the finding's significance (choice A)." },
];

